    "title": "Individual locomotor bias drives counterclockwise motion in pedestrian crowds",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19592341",
    "publication_date": "2026-04-15",
    "description": "<p>[*] SourceData.xlsx &mdash; Processed source data underlying each manuscript figure (Figures 1&ndash;8), organized one sheet per panel. Contains summary statistics, polarization distributions, velocity fields, social-norm survey counts, and individual-pedestrian laterality data derived from the raw experimental recordings.</p>\n<p>[*] ExperimentalData.zip &mdash; Raw trajectory data from all experiments, organized in four sub-folders:<br>- Spain/ (11 sessions, 63 CSV files) and Japan/ (10 sessions, 40 CSV files): crowd-walking experiments with adult pedestrians. Each file records per-frame pedestrian positions, velocities, and polarization (columns: Time, Id-Ped, X, Y, VX, VY, Pol).<br>- Teenagers/ (1 session) and Kids/ (4 sessions, 19 CSV files): equivalent recordings with younger age groups (same column format, without the Pol column).<br>- Individual/Trajectories/ (209 CSV files) and Individual/IndData-WithPolarization.xlsx: single-pedestrian experiment trajectories plus a participant-level spreadsheet with laterality attributes (handedness, footedness, eye dominance, sex, eye-patch condition) and individual polarization scores.</p>\n<p>[*] Codes.zip &mdash; Python scripts (figure_1e.py through figure_8.py, plus statistical_analysis.py) that reproduce all manuscript figures and statistical tests from SourceData.xlsx and ExperimentalData.zip.</p>",
